c)	Annotate StudentService with @Service and Student with @Component.
Aim: To register the target functional application source instances into the Core Spring Inversion of Control (IoC) framework context directory using specialized component stereotypes. 
.
Student Domain Model Bean (Student.java):
package com.example.demo.model;

import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;
@Component // Annotate Student with @Component
public class Student {
    private String name = "John Doe";
    private String rollNo = "251AI024";

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    public void setName(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    public String getRollNo() {
        return rollNo;
    }

    public void setRollNo(String rollNo) {
        this.rollNo = rollNo;
    }
}

Student Business Service Class Layer (StudentService.java):
package com.example.demo.service;

import com.example.demo.model.Student;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

@Service // Annotate StudentService with @Service
public class StudentService {

    @Autowired
    private Student student;

    public void displayStudentDetails() {
        System.out.println("[Service Method] Core logic: Student name is " + student.getName() + " with Roll Series: " + student.getRollNo());
    }
    public void updateStudentName(String newName) {
        System.out.println("[Service Method] Core logic: Modifying current name fields to: " + newName);
        student.setName(newName);
    }
}

d)	Implement AOP advice using @Aspect and @Before.
Aim: To define cross-cutting modular logic components that execute transparently before explicit business implementation join points run.

Logging Configuration Aspect Layer Component (LoggingAspect.java):
package com.example.demo.aspect;

import org.aspectj.lang.JoinPoint;
import org.aspectj.lang.annotation.Aspect;
import org.aspectj.lang.annotation.Before;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Aspect // Declares the component class as an isolated Aspect concern configuration
@Component
public class LoggingAspect {

    // Before advice configured globally across every executable signature found inside StudentService
    @Before("execution(* com.example.demo.service.StudentService.*(..))")
    public void logBeforeMethodCall(JoinPoint joinPoint) {
        String targetedMethodName = joinPoint.getSignature().getName();
        System.out.println("[AOP-BEFORE] Intercepting execution route! Triggering before: " + targetedMethodName);
    }
}

e)	Apply AOP advice to StudentService methods.
Aim: To link proxy configurations implicitly into the container runner using structural declarations.

Main Inversion-of-Control Configuration Class Entrypoint (DemoApplication.java):
package com.example.demo;

import org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.EnableAspectJAutoProxy;

@SpringBootApplication
@EnableAspectJAutoProxy // Forces the context runtime tracking engine to scan components tagged with @Aspect
public class DemoApplication {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(DemoApplication.class, args);
    }
}

f)	Write a test class to verify AOP functionality.
Aim: To test, run, and execute code assertions that confirm interceptors are applied securely and in the correct order.

JUnit Context Integration Test Verifier (StudentAopTest.java):
package com.example.demo;

import com.example.demo.service.StudentService;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.boot.test.context.SpringBootTest;

@SpringBootTest
public class StudentAopTest {

    @Autowired
    private StudentService studentService;

    @Test
    public void testAopAdviceInterception() {
        System.out.println("====== SYSTEM TEST INITIALIZATION ======");
        
        // Triggers advice interception hook immediately before standard execution block running
        studentService.displayStudentDetails();
        
   System.out.println("=========================================");
        
        // Confirms advice runtime layer intercepts parameter operations seamlessly
        studentService.updateStudentName("Alice Smith");
        System.out.println("========= SYSTEM TEST COMPLETED =========");
    }
}


